Keep std RTTI identity on non-MSVC: -fno-rtti + -fvisibility=hidden makes every
Yoga object emit weak private-external copies of std typeinfo it references
(_ZTISt9exception, _ZTISt11logic_error, ...). Linking libyogacore.a into a
dylib (libEngine.dylib) resolves the dylib's own references to those private
copies, and libc++abi matches catch clauses by typeinfo POINTER identity — so
every `catch (const std::exception&)` inside the dylib stops matching
libc++-thrown exceptions and the first real throw is std::terminate.
Catches on derived-most concrete types (e.g. std::filesystem::filesystem_error)
keep working because Yoga never emits those typeinfos.

MSVC keeps /GR-: it matches catch clauses by decorated type name, not typeinfo
address, so it never had the defect.

diff --git a/cmake/project-defaults.cmake b/cmake/project-defaults.cmake
--- a/cmake/project-defaults.cmake
+++ b/cmake/project-defaults.cmake
@@ -35,7 +35,5 @@ add_compile_options(
     # Enable warnings and warnings as errors
     -Wall
     -Werror
-    # Disable RTTI
-    $<$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>:-fno-rtti>
     # Use -O2 (prioritize speed)
     $<$<CONFIG:RELEASE>:-O2>
     # Enable separate sections per function/data item
